From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:59:07 -0400
Subject: base: Chrome's launched defaults, its key pins and certificate
 transparency

Chrome turns features on for every Stable user by server-side field trial,
which Stedding never receives, so a feature Chrome has launched stays off in
Stedding until upstream flips its default (BACKLOG S-236, found by comparing
Chrome Stable's seed with the pin's defaults, tooling/field-trials). This
patch turns on, each with a `Stedding (BACKLOG S-236)` comment:
StructuredHeadersInRust, DeprecateUnload and DeprecateUnloadByBucket
(Stedding's own chrome:// pages keep their unload handlers, as the permissions
policy already allows), AperitifHelpers (the Mac's helper processes; every
kind starts from the app bundle), PdfBufferedPaintManager,
IgnoreQuicCryptoConfigMemoryPressure, CheckAutoCommitInCommitAndRollback,
PaymentRequestRejectTooSmallWindows and TabSearchCjkWordBoundary.
TcpPortRandomizationMac stays off: the fix it needs is not in this pin.

Google's static key pins apply off iOS whatever the branding
(net/http/transport_security_state.cc); a pin list over ten weeks old turns
them off, and no violation is reported anywhere.

Certificate transparency is enforced (BACKLOG S-237): a public authority's
certificate must carry proof that it was logged, from the log list the
certificate component already brings, while a list over seventy days old
enforces nothing. The certificate audit reports Chrome sends with it stay off
in code: SCTReportingService always answers the disabled mode.

Tests: DefaultsTest.AFreshProfileHoldsAndWorksAfterStay checks every default
and that a web page's unload handler no longer runs while a chrome:// page's
still may; CertificateChecksTest.UnloggedAndUnpinnedCertificatesAreRefused
and CertificateReportsTest.NoCertificateIsReported, each failing with
Chromium's own code put back. SleepGateTest's unload page opts back in to
unload with a header.

Why: what every Chrome user has had for months, a safer and leaner browser,
should not be missing from Stedding because it arrives by a field trial.
Removable when: upstream turns each default on in code (re-read at every pin
move with tooling/field-trials), and drop this patch's hunks as they land.
