+// The certificate checks Chrome makes and Stedding makes too (BACKLOG S-236,
+// S-237; docs/PRIVACY.md), each seen on a navigation.
+//
+// Certificate Transparency: a public authority's certificate that was never
+// recorded in the public logs is refused while the log list is fresh. The
+// list comes with the certificate component updates, and the browser loads
+// it; a list more than ten weeks old enforces nothing, so a copy that has not
+// been updated keeps working. A root the user added (a company's, a debugging
+// proxy's) needs no log.
+//
+// Google's key pins: a certificate for a Google site that chains to a public
+// root Google did not pin is refused; one from a root the user added is not.
+//
+// Neither check reports anything: Chromium's sampled certificate reports to
+// Google stay off, whatever the Safe Browsing settings say.
